{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1120091-2e-site-based-devotions","id":1120091,"title":"[2E] Site Based Devotions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-24T14:58:13-07:00","id":1120091,"title":"[2E] Site Based Devotions","content":"Devotions that rely upon Locations meeting certain Conditions<br /> <br /> <b>Shekhina (Glorious Presence)</b><br /> Majesty \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Theban Sorcery \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> This is not a Theban Sorcery miracle but rather is a devotion that requires knowing Theban Sorcery and Majesty 5 to use at certain types of locations.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Vitae and 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> Be within a place which has the Resonant Condition (Holy), and has been so for the last century.<br /> <b>Action: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> Shekhina enhances Idol\u2019s aura of superiority from a divine one to the Divine One's. The vampire can wait until she\u2019s established Idol and then enhance it, or pay the price to immediately establish her superiority over everyone else in the room.<br /> Idol must already be in affect and those that succeed at a reflexive Resolve + Blood Potency \u2013 Majesty dots roll to be crass towards or spend Willpower to act against the Idol suffer the Blind Tilt as the vampire suddenly flares with divine glorious light. If the being that suffers the Blind Tilt from this also is a Kindred with less than half the Humanity as the user of Shekhina they also gain the Insensate Tilt from the agonizing pain.<br /> <br /> <b>Memory Biopsy</b><br /> Dominate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Wyrm Coil: Scale-Surgical Heart Removal<br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Extended Intelligence + Medicine roll with a target of ten successes and an interval of 1 minute<br /> <b>Requirement: </b>In a place that has the Anchor Condition of a Ghost that was a person who routinely performed lobotomies and other types of psychosurgical procedures. She must dip the tip of the biopsy needle with some of her Vitae or drip it onto scalpels that will be used to remove the brain matter. Only works on physically restrained corporeal undead.<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended 10 Successes, 1 Minute rolls<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> This Devotion extracts memories from Kindred and holds them within a small lump of the vampire's undead brain which is removed. The use of this power does not require the victim be Mesmerized. The vampire using this power must dip the tip of the biopsy needle with some of her Vitae or drip it onto scalpels that will be used to remove the brain matter. She can extract memories of an event, person, object, or location. If she deletes a broad swath of memories, the victim receives the Amnesia Condition. Supernatural attempts to recover or read the memories extracted by this method must succeed a Clash of Wills against the user which may be done if they have access to the part of the brain removed via this Devotion.<br /> Procedure: Over the course of about 15 minutes the Dragon uses a biopsy needle or scalpels to remove part of a Kindred subject\u2019s brain (which is customarily stored in a fermaldahyde jar). This process is both risky and demanding, requiring an extended Intelligence + Medicine roll with a target of ten successes and an interval of one minute. If successful, this procedure can be reversed with an identical roll by someone with this Devotion.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The brain of the subject is destroyed in the process. The shock is so terrible and sudden that the subject<br /> flies instantly into a mindless frenzy, essentually a draugr.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The area of the brain that holds the memories is damaged but the biopsy from the subject does not mystically contain the memories. The subject gains the Amnesia Condition as expected but it resolves itself the next night.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The memory which are being extracted is mystically held within the lumb of brain removed by the biopsy needle/scalpel. Contact with a container holding the tissue count as the same as touching the being for purposes of examining the memory psychically. The memory may not be recovered without adding the tissue back via this Devotion or an effect which does the same thing, which causes a Clash of Wills against the person who removed the memory. Should the body of the vampire whom donated the memories be destroyed that vampire will form as a rank 1 or 2 Ghost Anchored to the brain tissues and only remember the all the memories which it previously removed via this Devotion. This has resulted in a complete brain removal/memory extraction and subsequent final death creating a ghost of a vampire which remembered its life completely. Tissues extracted via this Devotion are instantly destroyed if removed from the location with the Anchored Condition which acted as the requirement for this Devotion to be used or if that Anchor Condtion is removed.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>All the normal benefits of an Exceptional Success on an extended roll, but nothing more.<br /> <br /> <b>King in his Castle</b><br /> Animalism \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Cost: </b>10 Vitae and 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> Be within a place which has the Infrastructure Condition (Sovereigny) in relation to the local population center which has been in place for the last decade, and is actively using Lord of the Land upon that building. Must have others within that population center that have the Fealty Oath Merit towards you.<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Until building loses the Infrastructure Condition (Sovereigny) or you leave it.<br /> All the Havens and Safe Places within the population center of those with the with Oath of Fealty Merit towards you are considered part of the area covered by Lord of the Land for the owner of the Haven/Safe Place and also for you. This means they gain the advantage of that Discipline use in regard of their places at the cost of their Lord also gaining it above them.<br /> <br /> <b>Anonymous Landscape</b><br /> Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae per Vampire (Spilt by others)<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <b>Requirement: </b>Be within a place which has the Infrastructure Condition (Juridical) in relation to the local population center which has been in place for the last decade and is considered a place to seek justice by the mortal populous. The vampire using this ability must have Lex Terras which is the building this is Devotion is used within and must have also Oubliette active.<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Until building loses the Infrastructure Condition (Juridical) or you leave it.<br /> Carthian Vampires with Lex Terras within your city may spill 1 Vitae within the building you have used this Devotion on to gain the benefits of Oubliette within the Feed Ground which is protected by Lex Terras during the night hours and maintain that benefit as long as you maintain the conditions of this Devotion. Those with Carthian status automatically see through the affects of this Devotion.<br /> <br /> <b>Steal the God's Form</b><br /> Dominate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Cruac Ritual \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> This is not a Cruac ritual but rather is a devotion that requires knowing Cruac Ritual and Dominate 5 to use at certain types of locations. This is a Devotion meant to allow a vampire to Possess a Spirit<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Vitae and 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Intelligence + Occult + Dominate \u2013 victim\u2019s Resistence + Rank<br /> <b>Requirement: </b>Be within a place which has the Open Condition to a Spirit which has the Materialized Condition. This location must also be a Locus. The vampire must have inflicted the Mesmerized Condition on the Spirit victim.<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 night per success.<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The victim\u2019s mind will not be bound to the vampire\u2019s control. He immediately resolves the Mesmerized Condition and regains a point of Willpower.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>The vampire cannot take total control of her victim just yet.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The vampire takes over her victim\u2019s Ephemeral form for one night<br /> per success. While in this new form, she uses her victim\u2019s Power, Finesse, and Resistence in place of her own Attributes and Skills. She can stay awake during the day by spending a point of Willpower at dawn and takes no damage from sunlight \u2014 if she does not spend Willpower, she returns to her body. Each night, she must spend a point of Vitae as normal. She cannot use Disciplines or Blood Sorcery when possessing someone else. She may use the spirits Manifestations, spending Vitae as if it were Essence to do so, but are not able to use any other supernatural abilities the being may have.<br /> If she attempts to kill herself, touch a bane of the spirit, or do something against the spirit's ban, the victim may roll Resistence + Rank as a reflexive action, on a success he evicts the vampire from his consciousness. Possessing a victim removes the Mesmerized and Dominated Conditions, and the vampire is not subject to any triggers set on the victim by Entombed Command while she remains in control. Once she leaves the victim\u2019s body, those triggers affect him as normal. While she commands the victim\u2019s body, the vampire\u2019s own form lies in a torpor-like state awaiting her return; if she remains in the victim\u2019s body for so long that her body slips into torpor, she immediately snaps back into her body.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The vampire slips into the victim\u2019s body with ease, and leaves her jaunt in another body with renewed purpose. Upon leaving the victim\u2019s body, she regains a point of Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-25-2017, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}